  "details": "When viewing the debug menu, if the current local avatar results in more than (roughly) 240 lines of either Parameters or Layers, then some information becomes inaccessible due to being unable to manually scroll between the 5 pages that PageUp, and PageDown seem to have access to.\n\nI have an example avatar uploaded that demonstrates this: https://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_f34f52d6-690c-4776-94df-1f9e1206e191\n\nThe avatar is the default example robot (with ears and tail & physbones removed) and it has 256 bools numbered 1-256 + the 28 default parameters.\n\nSwitch into the avatar, open the debug menu, and use PageDown, and PageUp to scroll around, notice that you can't see 16-28, 76-89, 137-150, and 198-210.\n\nIt seems that no matter what avatar you are in, the scrollbar will always scroll with 5 total pages, even if there isn't 5 pages worth of parameters. (either way less, or way more).",
